<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 16 March, from 597 BCE to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/597-bce">597 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,622 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nebuchadnezzar II captures Jerusalem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-chronicles">Babylonian Chronicle</a> records that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, carried <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehoiachin">King Jehoiachin</a> into exile and installed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zedekiah">Zedekiah</a>. A revolt led to the city's destruction in 587 BCE.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehoiachin">Jehoiachin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1355 CE <span class="tih-ago">671 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Han Lin'er is proclaimed emperor of a restored Song Dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Amid the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-turban-rebellion">Red Turban Rebellion</a> against the Yuan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-liner">Han Lin'er</a>, a claimed descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-huizong">Emperor Huizong</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>, was proclaimed emperor at Bozhou. He reigned in name only, with real power held first by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-futong">Liu Futong</a> and later by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Zhu Yuanzhang</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-turban-rebellion">Red Turban Rebellion</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1521">1521 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Magellan's expedition reaches the Philippines</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After crossing the Pacific, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan">Ferdinand Magellan</a>'s ships sighted Samar and landed at Homonhon. Magellan was killed on Mactan in April, but one ship completed the first circumnavigation in 1522.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1660">1660 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">366 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Long Parliament dissolves itself</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">First summoned in 1640, the Long Parliament voted its own dissolution and called new elections. The Convention Parliament that followed invited Charles II to return as king.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1802">1802 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">224 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress establishes the US Military Academy at West Point</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Jefferson signed the act founding a military academy at West Point, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. Its graduates included Grant, Lee and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1926">1926 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">100 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Goddard launches the first liquid-fuelled rocket</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Auburn, Massachusetts, Goddard's petrol and liquid-oxygen rocket flew for 2.5 seconds and rose about 12 metres. The principle underlies most modern space launch vehicles.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1935">1935 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">91 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler announces German rearmament and conscription</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Defying the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a>, Hitler reintroduced conscription and announced an army of 36 divisions. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> protested, but took no effective action.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US soldiers massacre villagers at My Lai</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American troops killed some 350 to 500 unarmed civilians, mostly women, children and old men, in a South Vietnamese hamlet. Exposed in 1969, the massacre deepened opposition to the war.</p></div></li></ol>
